<div class="pd-mediaplayer-documentation">

	<section id="overview">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Overview</h2>
		<p>
			<code>PDMediaPlayer</code> plays audio (and video) through the browser's own media element, with an
			accessible Bootstrap transport and <strong>markers</strong>: events along the timeline that are drawn on the
			seek bar, listed beside or beneath the player, filtered by kind and jumped between. It suits long
			recordings, such as radio shows, where the listener wants to speed up and to hop between points of interest.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Transport</strong>: play and pause, skip back and forward (15 and 30 seconds by default), a seek slider with the buffered ranges, time and duration, mute and volume, a speed menu and an optional download button.</li>
			<li><strong>Speed</strong>: 0.5× to 4× with the pitch preserved; the chosen speed is kept when the source changes, and can be remembered in local storage.</li>
			<li><strong>Markers</strong>: points or spans of any kind, coloured by kind, shown as ticks on the seek bar and in a virtualised list with the current marker highlighted.</li>
			<li><strong>Kind filter</strong>: a toggle chip per kind, with counts, hides or shows that kind everywhere, including next and previous.</li>
			<li><strong>Range</strong>: an optional shaded part of the seek bar (for example the show between its margins), with events as playback enters and leaves it. The audio is never trimmed.</li>
			<li><strong>Streaming</strong>: the element fetches the source itself, so a server that supports HTTP range requests lets the user seek anywhere without downloading the whole file.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="quick-start">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Quick Start</h2>

		<DocExample Title="Basic player"
					AnchorId="basic-player"
					Code="@_basicCode"
					Language="razor">
			<DemoContent>
				<PDMediaPlayer Src="@ShowUrl" Title="The breakfast show" />
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>Set <code>Src</code>. Everything else is optional.</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>

		<DocExample Title="Markers, range and speed"
					AnchorId="markers"
					Code="@_markersCode"
					Language="razor">
			<DemoContent>
				<PDMediaPlayer Src="@ShowUrl"
							   Markers="_markers"
							   KindLabels="_kindLabels"
							   SeekLead="TimeSpan.FromSeconds(3)"
							   RangeStart="TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5)"
							   RangeEnd="TimeSpan.FromSeconds(55)"
							   @bind-PlaybackRate="Rate"
							   OnMarkerSelected="m => Selected = m" />
				<p class="small text-muted mt-2 mb-0">Speed @Rate.ToString("0.##", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)×; selected: @(Selected?.Label ?? "none")</p>
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>
					Selecting a marker seeks <code>SeekLead</code> before it, so the lead-up can be heard, and raises
					<code>OnMarkerSelected</code>. Markers may be given in any order, may overlap, and may run past the
					end of the media (they are drawn at the end).
				</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>

		<DocExample Title="Controlling the player from code"
					AnchorId="api"
					Code="@_apiCode"
					Language="razor">
			<DemoContent>
				<p class="small text-muted mb-0">See the Demo tab, whose buttons call these methods.</p>
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>
					Every method can be called before the media is ready: a seek waits for the media to load, and a play
					request waits for the player's script.
				</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>
	</section>

	<section id="segments">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Segments</h2>

		<DocExample Title="Songs, talk and transcripts"
					AnchorId="segments-example"
					Code="@_segmentsCode"
					Language="razor">
			<DemoContent>
				<PDMediaPlayer Src="@ShowUrl"
							   Segments="_segments"
							   TranscriptExpanded="true"
							   OnSegmentEntered="s => NowPlaying = s.Label" />
				<p class="small text-muted mt-2 mb-0">Last segment entered: @(NowPlaying ?? "none")</p>
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>
					<code>PDMediaSegment</code>s are stretches of the timeline with a start and an end: songs, talking
					sections, adverts. They may overlap (overlaps are packed into extra lanes, up to
					<code>MaxSegmentLanes</code>) and may leave gaps. Segments whose end is not after their start are
					ignored, and segments past the end of the media are cut at the end. Each has <code>Id</code>,
					<code>Start</code>, <code>End</code>, <code>Kind</code>, <code>Label</code>, <code>Detail</code>,
					<code>Text</code> (plain text such as a transcript), <code>Lines</code> (timed
					<code>PDMediaTextLine</code>s with <code>Start</code>, <code>End</code>, <code>Text</code> and
					<code>Speaker</code>), <code>Lane</code>, <code>CssClass</code>, <code>Color</code>,
					<code>Confidence</code> and <code>Source</code>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Clicking a segment seeks to its start (less <code>SeekLead</code>); double clicking it, or its play
					button, plays just that segment and pauses at its end (within one position report, about a quarter
					of a second), and the loop button plays it over and over. The now playing strip shows the current
					segment, and its transcript pane highlights the line being spoken and keeps it in view; selecting a
					line seeks to it. <code>PDMediaSegment.FromMarkers</code> derives segments marker to marker, with
					options to skip kinds, end a segment with an end kind, and merge neighbours of the same kind.
				</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>
	</section>

	<section id="keyboard">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Keyboard</h2>
		<p>Shortcuts work only while focus is inside the player (never page wide), and not while the speed menu has focus.</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><kbd>K</kbd></td><td>Play or pause</td></tr>
				<tr><td><kbd>J</kbd> or <kbd>[</kbd></td><td>Previous marker</td></tr>
				<tr><td><kbd>L</kbd> or <kbd>]</kbd></td><td>Next marker</td></tr>
				<tr><td><kbd>M</kbd></td><td>Mute or unmute</td></tr>
				<tr><td><kbd>&lt;</kbd> and <kbd>&gt;</kbd></td><td>Next slower and next faster speed</td></tr>
				<tr><td><kbd>,</kbd> and <kbd>.</kbd></td><td>Previous and next segment</td></tr>
				<tr><td><kbd>P</kbd></td><td>Play the current segment on its own</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Arrow keys, <kbd>Page Up</kbd>, <kbd>Page Down</kbd>, <kbd>Home</kbd>, <kbd>End</kbd></td><td>Move the seek slider (it is a native range input)</td></tr>
				<tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd> on a list item</td><td>Select that marker</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>Presses with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>, <kbd>Alt</kbd> or <kbd>Meta</kbd> held, and held-down repeats, are ignored.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="parameters">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Parameters</h2>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Src</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td></td><td>URL of the media. Changing it resets position, duration and error, but keeps speed, volume and mute.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MediaKind</code></td><td><code>MediaKind</code></td><td><code>Audio</code></td><td>Audio or Video.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Poster</code>, <code>Title</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td></td><td>Video poster image; title, also the accessible name.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Preload</code></td><td><code>MediaPreload</code></td><td><code>Metadata</code></td><td>The element's preload attribute.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Autoplay</code>, <code>Loop</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>false</td><td>Start when ready; repeat at the end.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Muted</code>, <code>Volume</code></td><td><code>bool</code>, <code>double</code></td><td>false, 1</td><td>Two-way bindable.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShowDownload</code>, <code>DownloadUrl</code>, <code>DownloadFileName</code></td><td></td><td>false</td><td>Optional download button; the host decides the URL (for example an authorised endpoint), otherwise <code>Src</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SkipBackSeconds</code>, <code>SkipForwardSeconds</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>15, 30</td><td>Skip button distances.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>PlaybackRates</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;double&gt;?</code></td><td>0.75 to 2</td><td>The speed menu; values outside 0.5 to 4 are dropped.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>PlaybackRate</code></td><td><code>double</code></td><td>1</td><td>Two-way bindable speed; pitch is preserved.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Position</code></td><td><code>TimeSpan</code></td><td></td><td>Two-way bindable position; setting a new value seeks.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>StartAt</code></td><td><code>TimeSpan?</code></td><td></td><td>Seek here once each source loads (a remembered position wins).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>PersistKey</code>, <code>PersistInterval</code></td><td><code>string?</code>, <code>TimeSpan</code></td><td>null, 5 s</td><td>Remember the speed and the position (per source) in local storage, through a cascaded <code>PDLocalStorageStateManager</code> when there is one.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TimeUpdateRate</code></td><td><code>double</code></td><td>4</td><td>Position reports per second while playing (1 to 30).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>RangeStart</code>, <code>RangeEnd</code></td><td><code>TimeSpan?</code></td><td></td><td>Shade part of the seek bar.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Markers</code></td><td><code>IEnumerable&lt;PDMediaMarker&gt;?</code></td><td></td><td>The markers, in any order.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SeekLead</code></td><td><code>TimeSpan</code></td><td>0</td><td>Seek this far before a selected marker.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MarkerTolerance</code></td><td><code>TimeSpan</code></td><td>0.5 s</td><td>How close a marker may be before next and previous skip it; previous further into a marker than this returns to its start.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>VisibleKinds</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlySet&lt;string&gt;?</code></td><td>null (all)</td><td>Two-way bindable kind filter.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>KindLabels</code>, <code>KindColors</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyDictionary&lt;string, string&gt;?</code></td><td></td><td>Display names and CSS colours per kind.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShowKindFilter</code>, <code>ShowMarkerList</code>, <code>MarkerListExpanded</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>true</td><td>Show the chips and the list; start the list expanded.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MarkerListPlacement</code></td><td><code>MediaMarkerListPlacement</code></td><td><code>Below</code></td><td>Below or beside the player.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MarkerListMaxHeight</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>16rem</td><td>Height of the scrolling list.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MarkerTickResolution</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>400</td><td>Slots on the seek bar; markers of a kind in the same slot are drawn as one tick, and segments shorter than a slot merge.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Segments</code></td><td><code>IEnumerable&lt;PDMediaSegment&gt;?</code></td><td></td><td>The segments, in any order.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>VisibleSegmentKinds</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlySet&lt;string&gt;?</code></td><td>null (all)</td><td>Two-way bindable segment kind filter.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SegmentLanePlacement</code></td><td><code>MediaSegmentLanePlacement</code></td><td><code>Below</code></td><td>Lanes beneath or above the seek bar.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>MaxSegmentLanes</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>3</td><td>Lanes for overlapping segments; further overlaps share the last lane.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShowSegmentList</code>, <code>SegmentListExpanded</code>, <code>ShowNowPlaying</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>true</td><td>The segment list and the now playing strip.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TranscriptExpanded</code>, <code>TranscriptMaxHeight</code></td><td><code>bool</code>, <code>string</code></td><td>false, 10rem</td><td>The transcript pane.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShowErrors</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>true</td><td>Show a message in the player when the media cannot be played.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			<code>PDMediaMarker</code> has <code>Id</code>, <code>Position</code>, an optional <code>Length</code> (a span
			rather than a point), <code>Kind</code> (such as <code>dead-air</code>), <code>Label</code>, <code>Detail</code>,
			<code>CssClass</code> and <code>Color</code>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="methods">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Methods</h2>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>PlayAsync</code>, <code>PauseAsync</code>, <code>TogglePlayAsync</code></td><td>Playback.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SeekAsync(TimeSpan)</code>, <code>SkipAsync(TimeSpan)</code></td><td>Seek to, or by, a time; limited to the media.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SeekToMarkerAsync(PDMediaMarker)</code></td><td>Seek to a marker (less <code>SeekLead</code>) and raise <code>OnMarkerSelected</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>NextMarkerAsync(string? kind)</code>, <code>PreviousMarkerAsync(string? kind)</code></td><td>Jump relative to the position; without a kind, only visible kinds count. Returns the marker, or null.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SetPlaybackRateAsync</code>, <code>SetVolumeAsync</code>, <code>SetMutedAsync</code>, <code>ToggleMuteAsync</code></td><td>Speed and sound.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SetKindVisibleAsync(string, bool)</code>, <code>IsKindVisible(string)</code></td><td>The kind filter.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SeekToSegmentAsync(PDMediaSegment)</code></td><td>Seek to a segment (less <code>SeekLead</code>) and raise <code>OnSegmentSelected</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>NextSegmentAsync(string? kind)</code>, <code>PreviousSegmentAsync(string? kind)</code></td><td>Jump between segment starts; returns the segment, or null.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>PlaySegmentAsync(PDMediaSegment, bool loop)</code>, <code>SetSegmentLoopAsync(bool)</code></td><td>Play one segment and stop (or loop) at its end.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SetSegmentKindVisibleAsync(string, bool)</code>, <code>IsSegmentKindVisible(string)</code></td><td>The segment kind filter.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			Read-only properties: <code>CurrentPosition</code>, <code>Duration</code>, <code>IsReady</code>, <code>IsLive</code>,
			<code>IsPlaying</code>, <code>CurrentPlaybackRate</code>, <code>CurrentVolume</code>, <code>IsMuted</code>,
			<code>LastError</code>, <code>CurrentMarker</code>, <code>SortedMarkers</code>, <code>VisibleMarkers</code>,
			<code>CurrentSegment</code>, <code>CurrentSegments</code>, <code>SortedSegments</code>, <code>VisibleSegments</code>,
			<code>PlayingSegment</code>, <code>IsLoopingSegment</code>.
		</p>
	</section>

