			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>OnReady</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;TimeSpan?&gt;</code></td><td>The duration is known (null for a live stream).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnTimeUpdate</code>, <code>PositionChanged</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;TimeSpan&gt;</code></td><td>The position, throttled to <code>TimeUpdateRate</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnPlay</code>, <code>OnPause</code>, <code>OnEnded</code></td><td><code>EventCallback</code></td><td>Playback state.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnError</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;MediaPlayerError&gt;</code></td><td>A friendly reason: 401, 403, 404, server error, network, decode or unsupported format.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnMarkerSelected</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;PDMediaMarker&gt;</code></td><td>A marker was selected by any means.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnRangeEntered</code>, <code>OnRangeLeft</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;TimeSpan&gt;</code></td><td>Playback crossed into or out of the shaded range.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnSegmentSelected</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;PDMediaSegment&gt;</code></td><td>A segment was selected by any means.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnSegmentEntered</code>, <code>OnSegmentLeft</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;PDMediaSegment&gt;</code></td><td>Playback or a seek crossed a segment boundary; raised for each of overlapping segments, whatever the kind filter.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>PlaybackRateChanged</code>, <code>VolumeChanged</code>, <code>MutedChanged</code>, <code>VisibleKindsChanged</code>, <code>VisibleSegmentKindsChanged</code></td><td></td><td>For two-way binding.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section id="performance">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Many markers</h2>
		<p>
			The marker list is virtualised (only the rows in view are rendered). On the seek bar, the bar is divided into
			<code>MarkerTickResolution</code> slots and markers of the same kind (and colour and class) that fall in the
			same slot, or overlap a span already drawn there, are merged into one tick whose tooltip gives the count. So
			at most that many ticks per kind are drawn, whether there are ten markers or ten thousand. Next, previous
			and the current marker use binary search over the sorted markers.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="errors">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Errors and live streams</h2>
		<p>
			A media element does not reveal the HTTP status of its request. When loading fails with a network or format
			error, the player asks the server for the first byte of the source to tell a refused (401 or 403) or missing
			(404) file from a genuinely unplayable one, and reports a <code>MediaPlayerError</code> with a friendly
			message. A source whose duration is infinite (a live stream) disables the seek bar and the skip buttons, and
			<code>OnReady</code> receives null.
		</p>
	</section>

</div>

<section>
	<h2>Notes and piano roll</h2>
	<p>Set ShowNotes to true and supply Notes as PDMediaNote items with Start, Duration, MidiNote, Voice, Color and Label.
		The optional lane shares the media time axis and adds octave pitch names, a playback cursor and buttons that seek to each note.
		HiddenNoteVoices filters voice identifiers using ordinal comparison. It changes the display only; provide matching audio when muting a voice.
		Notes are off by default. Nonpositive durations, negative starts and pitches outside MIDI 0 to 127 are ignored; notes are clipped to the media duration.</p>
</section>
